1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,459
People born without a working C5 protein

2
00:00:03,259 --> 00:00:06,401
get meningococcal infections, again and again.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,497
Eculizumab is a drug that blocks C5.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,210
Its label opens with a boxed warning:

5
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:14,360
serious meningococcal infections.

6
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,025
The disease predicted the side effect.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,122
Knockout turns that into a method.

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,427
A drug that blocks a protein is a chemical knockout.

9
00:00:25,227 --> 00:00:28,471
It should cause a milder form of that protein's disease.

10
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,823
Ask it in plain words:

11
00:00:30,623 --> 00:00:33,669
what side effects should a C5 blocker cause?

12
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,108
The Fetch.ai orchestrator finds five approved C5 blockers

13
00:00:37,908 --> 00:00:39,474
and picks eculizumab.

14
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:43,229
The target agent reads what the drug acts on,

15
00:00:43,029 --> 00:00:45,167
and which way, from ChEMBL.

16
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:49,613
The genetics agent finds the disease where C5 fails the same way,

17
00:00:49,413 --> 00:00:50,662
and its symptoms.

18
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:54,059
The label and report agents check each symptom

19
00:00:53,859 --> 00:00:55,619
against the FDA's records.

20
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,334
Today those two answer unknown:

21
00:00:58,134 --> 00:01:01,579
mapping symptoms to report terms needs a Gemini key.

22
00:01:01,379 --> 00:01:05,073
They say which step failed, and never call unknown safe.

23
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,613
The report page shows the same chain from the live API,

24
00:01:13,413 --> 00:01:15,599
down to three predicted effects.

25
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,948
They're not checked yet,

26
00:01:17,748 --> 00:01:21,712
so we checked the meningococcal one by hand with the engine's code,

27
00:01:21,512 --> 00:01:23,622
and show it in the page's fixture.

28
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:28,050
The boxed warning matches word for word.

29
00:01:27,850 --> 00:01:32,449
86 of 54,046 eculizumab reports name the infection,

30
00:01:32,249 --> 00:01:34,864
against 311 in 20.7 million.

31
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:38,964
A proportional reporting ratio of 146.

32
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,243
One example proves nothing,

33
00:01:42,043 --> 00:01:45,165
so the measurement was fixed before any scoring.

34
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,235
A script picks the drugs: 52 approved drugs

35
00:01:48,035 --> 00:01:51,727
whose target has a genetic disease pointing the same way.

36
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:57,011
Label precision comes first, then the lift over 100 shuffled diseases.

37
00:01:56,811 --> 00:01:58,523
Neither is measured yet;

38
00:01:58,323 --> 00:02:01,044
scoring waits on that same mapping step.

39
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,791
A blank beats a number we didn't measure.

40
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,526
Every prediction is stored in Tiger Data with its cited chain.

41
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,489
A database trigger refuses any prediction

42
00:02:13,289 --> 00:02:15,388
that arrives without its evidence.

43
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:19,122
A prediction found in the reports but not on the label

44
00:02:18,922 --> 00:02:22,301
becomes a candidate new signal, shown with its caveats.

45
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,529
Reports keep arriving, so a Creao watch agent

46
00:02:27,329 --> 00:02:29,834
re-counts each watched drug by quarter

47
00:02:29,634 --> 00:02:31,471
and posts the changes back.

48
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,926
This run used live counts and a hand-picked term:

49
00:02:35,726 --> 00:02:38,816
still above the threshold, at PRR 146.

50
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,216
New at LA Hacks, on Helix's catalog:

51
00:02:45,016 --> 00:02:49,721
the pipeline, both checks, the agents, the watch and the page.

52
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,639
A drug is only a partial knockout,

53
00:02:52,439 --> 00:02:55,273
so its effects may be milder, or absent.

54
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:58,467
Every genetic disease already ran the trial.
